(:id "port/python/vt/cook-open" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/open" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/negative-controls" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_surfaces_test.go: TestPythonCookForeignAndForgerySurfaces" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_open_scale_test.go: TestPythonCookOpenFunctionalScale" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_guard_storage_test.go: TestPythonCookInactiveGuardStorage" "make python-cook-test (make/python-cook.mk)" "make python-cook-negative-control (make/python-cook.mk)" "make dist-python") :tested-revision "013425a08b7b1980bd5609c23384e7e9e02527dc" :note "2026-11-17: open_cook checks the header words, the derived data offset, the file equation and the base's residue and nothing per node; check_cook runs cook-check's two passes. TestPythonCook/open holds the runtime's verdict to cook-check's name on the tool's cooks and every forged header, directory, storage and reference row (a big-endian cook refuses foreign_order on this little-endian host); the cook, cook-foreign and cook-forgery conformance surfaces pass under both pins; sparse 1 MiB to 1 GiB cooks open in the same time. Controls: the reserved-word check removed from a copy of _schema/cook.py, file-size work planted into open, and the per-test storage controls each go red. Run on macOS arm64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 built into dist/ by make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision; the open-scale and shape gates also ran on Linux x86-64.")
(:id "port/python/vt/cook-write" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/write" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_test.go: TestPythonCook/negative-controls" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_cpp_test.go: TestPythonCookCppIdentity" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_fixedclass_test.go: TestPythonCookFixedClass" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_padding_test.go: TestPythonCookCountedUnionPadding" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_refusal_test.go: TestPythonCookRefusals" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_surfaces_test.go: TestPythonCookForeignAndForgerySurfaces" "internal/codegen/pythontable/cook_shape_test.go: TestPythonCookShapeFunctional" "make python-cook-test (make/python-cook.mk)" "make python-cook-negative-control (make/python-cook.mk)" "make dist-python") :tested-revision "013425a08b7b1980bd5609c23384e7e9e02527dc" :note "2026-11-17: cook writes tablecook.Cook's file byte for byte in both byte orders for every probe unit, and cook_measure equals the file length; the cook-write surface passes under both pins and the C++ identity rows match the generated C++ cook. Dead slots, inactive arm storage and padding are zero: a writer whose buffer starts non-zero fails TestPythonCook/write at the first dead byte, and TestPythonCookFixedClass. A write validates first and raises InvalidValue in every run (no assert carries it): with the validation removed TestPythonCookRefusals, TestPythonCookRequiredRange and TestPythonCookUnionFloat go red. The built-in controls move the byte order, the wide integer's order, the pointer delta and the attribution length in a copy of _schema/cookwrite.py and each comparison goes red. Run on macOS arm64 with CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 built into dist/ by make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
